course: dictionary
lesson: 4312
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word groove can mean a narrow cut in a surface, or a good rhythm in music. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants. Look for clues about tyres, wet roads, water, music or dancing.
explain: «The grooves in a tyre's tread push water away so the tyre can grip.» Grooves here are narrow channels cut into the rubber. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The narrow channels in a tyre's tread push water away" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Music words are often informal, so they have a different job. When a song has a great groove, the word means a rhythm that makes you want to move. Check the context first, because the same word can mean a cut in one sentence and a beat in another.
fact: A groove is a long, narrow cut or channel in a surface.
fact: «The thorny devil has tiny grooves between its spines that pull water from damp sand up to its mouth.»
fact: In the UK, the minimum tread depth for cars is 1.6 millimetres, and on wet roads cars need much longer to stop.
fact: Informally, a groove is a good rhythm in music, and to groove means to move to music in a relaxed, happy way.
fact: Being «in the groove» means doing something smoothly and well.
exercise: «The grooves in a tyre's tread push water away so the tyre can grip.» What do the grooves do? | *Push water away so the tyre can grip | Make the tyre sing like a song | Hold the tyre still | Make the car go faster on dry roads
exercise: «The thorny devil has tiny grooves between its spines that pull water from damp sand up to its mouth.» Find and copy one word that means a narrow cut. | devil | spines | sand | *grooves
exercise: Ava says, «The band had a great groove, and everyone started to dance.» What does groove mean here? | A cut in a surface | A kind of tyre | *A good rhythm in music that makes you want to dance | A long, deep hole in the ground
test: «The car's tyres grip the wet road through their grooves.» What does grooves mean here? | Gentle hills | Dancing steps | A type of music | *Narrow channels in the tyre
test: What does it mean to groove? | To drive very fast on a wet road | To cut a deep hole in wood | *To move to music in a relaxed, happy way | To be sad and tired
exam: «A pencil is a rod of graphite mixed with clay, baked, laid in grooves between two thin slats of cedar wood.» Which meaning fits best here? | A good rhythm for dancing | *A narrow channel cut into the wood | Something to eat | To move slowly through the water
